# Commission: What does retaining a theory buy beyond keeping the fix?

## Intended contribution

Replace the old lead's body from scratch with a short outward-facing companion to the current lead. Give a technical maintainer a way to tell whether it is worth paying to retain and test an explanation alongside a winning patch. Reader should see three separable bets and a comparison that can distinguish each, including negative or mixed results. Suggested eventual reader-facing title: What Does a Learning System Gain by Retaining a Theory Rather Than Just the Fix? Keep the current H1 unchanged for the rewrite guard; retitling/relocation is a subsequent editorial operation, not part of this worker's task. The new article must work on its own. Update description and source_notes to match the new contribution.

## Must keep

One explicitly hypothetical running example: README feeds a client's build; retained method to inspect configured build inputs rather than ignore all docs; a later failure through an indirect include exposes the assumption that the list is exhaustive. Follow what the system actually does differently on the next investigation, including what observation or discriminating test could overturn its diagnosis. Show the three bets in the course of the investigation: (1) same raw failure evidence to the proposer, with/without formulated diagnosis, match budget and count diagnosis costs; benefit of supplying a diagnosis does not show autonomous discovery of it; (2) direct criticism at a separable premise vs an undifferentiated account while holding edit options open, check that retained claims still work on prior and fresh cases; (3) carry tested account across jobs vs reconstruct from the same accessible case history with the same base model and patch; compare new target observations to a common performance threshold and total cost at comparable quality, which can diverge. Do not force patch-only baseline to fail to think, and don't make availability proof that the retained account drove the result. Include how to challenge or withhold a premise while keeping the patch fixed. Distinguish changing a theory about a client from doing research on one's own development method; selection of a self-edit need not be theory building. Show a mixed result, like less reconstruction time but no fewer new observations. Keep conjectural status, provenance and limits beside the claim.

## Must exclude

No duplicate deployment-time learning introduction, long historical/formalization/Gödel/Naur argument, Bitter Lesson defense, universal interpretability claim, compounding discussion, list of supplements, new study results or implementation. Do not rebuild old text to preserve backlinks; identify material displaced in writer report. No need to quote outside literature when explaining this explicitly hypothetical comparison. Prefer concrete consequences to abstract three-part labels. Aim for 750–1100 words, shorter if complete.

## Reserved decisions

Scope one article, not the lead or testing supplements, navigation or any other concurrent work. Keep byline, status, banner and (only for this guarded stage) H1 and path. No movement or publication by workers. Whether to promote exact text and relocate is for the operator.

## Current direction

The operator accepted rewriting the previous theory-builder lead as a focused companion about the value of retaining an account of why a change works. Distill what is genuinely worth salvaging and don't make 'theory builder' the umbrella name for all reflective self-improvement by selection.
